Package: MEForLab
Type: Package
Title: Common Analysis Procedures, Forestry Functions, and Growth Projection Tools for the Maine Forest Lab
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person("Mike", "Premer", email = "michael.premer@maine.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Forestry functions used at the Maine Forest Management Lab,
    University of Maine (stand density, competition indices, site index,
    volume, crown width, wind risk), plus tools to turn inventory data into
    tree lists and project them forward with either the FVS Remodeling
    Project's variant-free CONUS equations (implemented in R) or a compiled
    Forest Vegetation Simulator variant. See maineforestlab.com.
License: GPL-2
Encoding: UTF-8
LazyData: true
Depends: R (>= 4.1)
Imports: stats, utils, graphics
Suggests: readxl, RSQLite, DBI, ggplot2, dplyr, tidyr, sf, raster, topmodel,
    knitr, rmarkdown, testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
RoxygenNote: 7.3.2
